}
table_lines <- c(
  table_lines, "",
  "Common support is the intersection of the fitted propensity-score ranges for NSW treated and CPS controls, estimated separately for each covariate set. All 185 treated observations were inside that intersection in both models; trimming therefore only removes CPS controls. The displayed CPS N is the candidate pool, not the number of distinct controls selected by matching.",
  "",
  "For 1-NN rows, MatchIt forms ATT matches with replacement. Standard errors use an Abadie--Imbens-style analytic conditional-variance estimator with three same-arm nearest neighbours for local outcome variances and control reuse counts; no ordinary bootstrap is used. Stratification uses five score strata defined by treated-score quintiles and a fixed-strata sampling variance. These intervals do not propagate uncertainty from estimating the propensity-score model."
